# Firmware upload = PlatformIO Remote only

The Nano ESP32 is on the **remote agent machine**, not this PC. Local USB/DFU upload will fail with "No DFU capable USB device".

**Never** run `pio run -t upload` (or any local upload) for this project.

**Always** use:

```bash
pio remote --agent desktop-o1gdd79 run --force-remote -e arduino_nano_esp32 -t upload
```

from `antenna-tracker/`. If agents are missing, tell the user to start `pio remote agent start` on the agent PC, then retry. Do not fall back to local DFU unless the user explicitly asks.
